The "systematic pattern without unified intent" reading: When I suggested (for 8a) that individuals weren't purposefully thwarting God's cosmic plan, I may have imposed modern assumptions about distributed systems onto an ancient text that might assume more unified collective intent. The text's "she rebelled" might indicate more conscious collective opposition than I allowed.\
Too quick to see non-metaphysical accountability: The text's silence on consciousness/soul requirements doesn't necessarily mean they're irrelevant - it might simply assume them. Ancient readers might have taken for granted that Jerusalem-as-entity had some kind of collective 
